  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The advanced sunburst adds a fourth round of five-treble "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [{ "type": "glossaryTooltip", "attrs": { "termSlug": "shell-stitch" } }],
            "text": "shells"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to the three-round basic version, taking the motif from 10 cm to 14 cm and filling the open chain arches with a fanning border. Rounds 1 through 3 match the basic sunburst exactly, so both sizes can be worked from the same starting sequence before diverging at round 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Two-colour working reads most clearly: rounds 1 and 2 in the spoke colour (the rays), round 3 onward in the border colour (the halo). Single-colour gives a more unified look. The shells in round 4 close the motif enough to join in a grid rather than a honeycomb."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Materials for one motif",
          "body": "About 14 g of DK-weight cotton in one or two colours. A 4 mm crochet hook (UK 8, US G/6). Tapestry needle. Scissors. Blocking mat and pins."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Gauge" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each finished advanced sunburst measures 14 cm across at widest point in DK-weight cotton with a 4 mm hook, after a steam-block. The shells expand considerably with blocking, so measure after blocking rather than before."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Stitches used" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "chain (ch) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "slip stitch (sl st) — UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "double crochet (dc) — UK; US \"single crochet\"." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "treble cluster (3tr-cl) — three trebles drawn together at the top. UK; US \"3dc-cl\"." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "shell (5tr in same st) — five trebles into the same base stitch. UK and US shared." }] }] },
          { "type": "listItem", "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "magic ring (MR) — adjustable starting loop." }] }] }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pattern" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked in the round, right side facing throughout. Do not turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Rounds 1 and 2" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work rounds 1 and 2 exactly as the basic sunburst motif. At the end of round 2: 6 clusters, 6 ch-4 arches."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 3" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 1 (does not count as a stitch). Dc into top of first cluster. Ch 2. Work 4dc into next ch-4 arch. Ch 2. *Dc into top of next cluster. Ch 2. Work 4dc into next ch-4 arch. Ch 2.* Repeat from * to * four more times. Sl st to first dc to join. (36 dc, 12 ch-2 spaces.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 3 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 4" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join contrast colour if changing. Ch 1. Dc into first dc (the single cluster-top dc from round 3). Work 5tr into next ch-2 space (shell made). Dc into next dc (first of the 4dc group). Sk 2dc. Work 5tr into next ch-2 space (second shell). Dc into last dc of the group. *Dc into single cluster-top dc. Work 5tr shell into next ch-2 sp. Dc into first 4dc-group dc. Sk 2dc. Work 5tr shell into next ch-2 sp. Dc into last 4dc-group dc.* Repeat from * to * four more times. Sl st to first dc to join. (12 shells with 5tr each, 12 dc.) Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chart" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The chart reads outward from the magic ring. Rounds 1 to 3 match the basic sunburst chart. Round 4 adds the shell symbols fanning between each spoke group."
          }
        ]
      },
