      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Finishing" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fasten off all colour ends, leaving 15 cm tails. Weave each tail through 3 to 4 stitches on the back of the nearest round, then back through 2 to 3 stitches in the opposite direction. Trim. Steam-block firmly, pinning the tips of each shell outward to maximise the width."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Joining" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join through the dc stitches between shells using whipstitch through back loops only. Because the shells fill the outer rim, tiles join without gaps in a straight grid, making this version better suited to blankets than the basic sunburst."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Care" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash in cool water with a small amount of mild soap, or machine-wash on a wool cycle. Do not tumble-dry. Lay flat on a clean towel and ease to shape while damp."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "What to try next" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mix the basic (10 cm) and advanced (14 cm) sunburst sizes for a staggered throw with built-in scale variation. The African flower three-colour motif (crochet-african-flower-three-colour) uses a similar six-petal structure with puff stitches at the spoke tips."
          }
        ]
      }
